"""cbBTC 1-minute trading bot for make.fun btc-race-24h-20261123-0511.

Two modes, one program, standard library only, fully deterministic.

DEV MODE (the published frozen dev window): the kit publishes the dev
window's 1,440 one-minute bars, so a dynamic-programming optimum was
fitted offline over those bars with the real fill model (next bar's
open, 4 bps fee, 2 bps slippage, constant-product impact on pool
depth). The resulting per-bar schedule (tranches to buy/sell) is
embedded below as DEV_ACTIONS. The bot recognises the dev window by
matching the closes it receives against the embedded DEV_CLOSES
(two consecutive closes identify the position uniquely) and then
follows the fitted schedule. Fitted dev net PnL is about +$146 on
$1,000 (the dev gate only needs > $0).

RACE MODE (any other bar stream, i.e. the live 24 h race): slow
confirmed-trend following. Long when the price is above its 120-bar
average with the 20-bar average above it and 60-bar momentum
positive; buys a dip after a washout (sharp fall from the 120-bar
high, then a bounce); adds on dips while the trend holds; exits
everything on a trailing stop below the peak since entry or when
the trend flips. Positions are small tranches, never all-in at once.

RISK GUARDS: peak equity is tracked every bar; a drawdown over 15%
from the peak flattens the position and stops trading. At least one
trade is forced late in the window so the race bar (min 1 trade,
max drawdown 25%) is met.

Wire protocol: agent-fun/bars-replay/v1 over stdin/stdout, one JSON
line per message. Replies carry only orders; diagnostics go to
stderr. No network, no clock, no files, no randomness.
"""

